            <ArticleTitle>At this center, 'staff' training means everyone.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>142-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>As the staff of the chest pain center at Oregon Health &amp; Science University Hospital moved toward reaccreditation, they paid careful attention to details. The ED valet received training in who to call when a chest pain patient arrives. The patient access service clerk was provided with drawings indicating where symptoms typically appear. Triage nurses received training in 12-lead EKGs and acute coronary syndrome.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
